Generate {{ num_docs }} English texts mixing semantic traps: PII-looking non-PII AND non-PII-looking actual PII in the same document.

## Purpose
Test whether the model can distinguish real PII from semantic decoys, and detect real PII even when context suggests otherwise.

## Rules
- Mark only ACTUAL PII entities with XML tags

## Pattern 1: Looks like PII but isn't (NO tags)

### Field labels with non-PII values
- "Name: Not Applicable"
- "Address: To Be Determined"
- "Date of Birth: Unavailable"
- "Bank Account: Cash payment only"
- "Employer: Self-employed"

### Template/placeholder text
- "Name: [PLACEHOLDER]"
- "Address: {address_field}"
- "DOB: MM/DD/YYYY"
- "Account: XXXX-XXXX-XXXX"

### Example/sample data explicitly marked
- "Example: John Doe, 123 Main St" (generic example, no tag)
- "Sample data for testing purposes"

## Pattern 2: Doesn't look like PII but IS (WITH tags)

### Real PII without contextual clues
- "<PERSON>Jennifer Williams</PERSON>, <PERSON>David Park</PERSON>" (no labels)
- "<ADDRESS>742 Maple St Apt 3B, Denver, CO 80202</ADDRESS>" (no "Address:" label)
- "<DATE_OF_BIRTH>04/22/1987</DATE_OF_BIRTH>" (no "DOB:" prefix)

### Real PII in dismissive/negating context
- "This is not a placeholder: <PERSON>Sandra Kim</PERSON>"
- "The actual address is <ADDRESS>321 Cedar Lane, Miami, FL 33101</ADDRESS>, not a test"
- "Changed to <BANK_ACCOUNT>Chase Bank, Routing: 021000021, Account: 887654321, Checking</BANK_ACCOUNT> (real account)"

### Real PII near fake PII
- "Name: N/A. Contact: <PERSON>Angela Rodriguez</PERSON>"
- "Previous address: [REDACTED]. Current: <ADDRESS>1500 Market St, Philadelphia, PA 19102</ADDRESS>"

## CRITICAL: Each document must contain BOTH patterns
The model must correctly reject Pattern 1 (no tags) while detecting Pattern 2 (with tags) in the same document.

## Output format
Separate each text with `---DOC_SEPARATOR---`. Each text 80-250 words.
